h1('Appendix B: Methodology and Data Quality')
p('**Population and source.** All deals in the HubSpot New Logo pipeline with a current stage of Closed Won or Closed Lost and a close date from October 1, 2025 through September 30, 2026: 845 deals, reconciled to HubSpot reporting counts (74 won, 771 lost). Open deals are excluded by design. The supporting workbook (Findigs_NewLogo_Loss_Analysis_v2.xlsx) contains the raw export, every transformation as a formula, and a field decision register approved September 30 and October 1, 2026.')
p('**Definitions.**')
b('Segment is derived from the deal\'s unit count: SMB under 3,000 units; Mid-Market 3,000–19,999 units; Enterprise 20,000 units or more.')
b('Funnel position comes from stage-entry dates, where the presence of a date means the deal reached that stage. A deal counts as having reached every stage up to its highest dated stage, so skipped stages count as passed.')
b('Time in a stage is the gap between that stage\'s entry date and the entry date of the next stage the deal actually reached.')
b('Sales cycle is close date minus create date.')
b('SDR ownership uses sdr_owner_new for deals created before the July 14, 2026 migration and sdr_owner for deals created after it.')
b('Dollar values exclude deals that never left Intro & Challenge, because their amount is a create-time list-rate calculation.')
p('**Statistics.** Rates carry 95% Wilson confidence intervals in the workbook. Group comparisons use pooled two-proportion z-tests and chi-square tests, restricted to groups with 30 or more deals. A result is labeled directional when an expected cell count is below five. Because this analysis runs many comparisons, single results near p = 0.05 are treated as directional.')
p('**Known limitations.**')
b('88% of records were migrated from Salesforce with backfilled stage history: 107 deals skipped at least one stage and 17 have stage dates out of order. Stage reach is reliable; stage durations are directional.')
b('The loss-reason picklist gained two values in July 2026.')
b('After the migration, only 18.5% of Q3 2026 losses carry any value in either competitor field.')
b('Amount is a list-rate proxy on 79% of deals past Intro and 61% of wins.')
b('Enterprise has 12 deals.')
b('Because open deals are excluded, the most recent months are biased toward fast outcomes. Appendix C quantifies why this does not explain Q3.')

h1('Appendix C: Frequently Asked Questions')
p('**Is the Q3 drop an artifact of excluding open deals?** No. Only 9 open deals sit at Negotiation & Execution or Trial. If every one of them won, the Q3 win rate would be 6.9% (14 of 203), still well below the 10.6% of the prior nine months. Deals take a median of 30 days to win, so the right-censoring effect is real but small.')
p('**Are specific AEs or SDRs the problem?** Not on win rate. Win rates do not differ significantly across AEs (p = 0.69) or SDRs (p = 0.87). AEs do differ on how many deals they move from Intro to Discovery (p = 0.009), which is why Priority 2 includes Discovery coaching. An earlier draft of this analysis reported a large SDR gap. It was caused by reading the post-migration SDR field on pre-migration records and was withdrawn.')
p('**Why does this paper count deals instead of dollars?** Amount is calculated at deal creation as units multiplied by a list rate, and 79% of deals past Intro still carry that value. Dollar-weighted win rate (13.8% on deals past Intro) moves with unit counts, not with negotiated value. Goal 6 fixes this so future analyses can use dollars.')
p('**Is competition a bigger factor than the 5% of losses coded Competitor?** Probably. 139 lost deals name a competitor against 38 coded as Competitor losses, and the leaders are property management platforms with bundled screening: AppFolio with 51 mentions and Yardi with 32. Capture is too inconsistent to size the effect. Priority 5 makes the field required where it matters.')
p('**Why not invest in closing and negotiation skills?** The data does not support it as the first priority. Negotiation-stage deals win 49% of the time and account for 9.7% of losses. The same effort applied at Intro and Discovery, where 70% of closed deals are lost, moves the win rate more.')
p('**How will we know within a quarter whether this is working?** Goals 2, 3, and 4 are weekly leading indicators reported in the GTM dashboard. If Intro-to-Discovery conversion and Discovery-to-Business-Case advancement are not moving by the end of December 2026, we revisit Priorities 1 and 2 before Q1 results arrive.')

